3.1 Vehicle model
The vehicle model part represents the dynamic response of the vehicle to a steering angle α in terms of lateral deviation y relative to the road centerline (ﬁgure 6).
The planar dynamics of the vehicle are modeled using a ﬁrst-order approximation of the classical ‘bicycle model’ [10]. It is assumed that this overly simpliﬁed model is representative of the internal model that drivers actually use to adjust their steering to enter a curve.

