3.3 Motor control
The motor control model part represents the desired steering angle applied to the wheel to achieve an actual steer angle α.
The ‘crossover’ model of McRuer [19] for visuo-motor tasks is used. This model is based on the observation that the transfer function G of a coupled system composed of an operator H manipulating a system S is: G = H · S = ωc(e−Ts/s), where ωc is the natural crossover frequency of S and T is a neuromuscular response time. This model therefore expresses the adaptation of the operator’s response to the dynamics of the system and yields the following operator transfer function H = S−1ωc(e−Ts/s).
